# peeryard patch ergo/004: Do not start full block download inside a NiPoPoW headers gap
# upstream: ergoplatform/ergo#2596 (proposed); origin, witness and responses in patches.json
From a9caba652058a6f62af84e2e932b0aecb20dc0d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cafebedouin <cafebedouin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:55:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Do not start full block download inside a NiPoPoW headers gap

A pruned digest node bootstrapped from a NiPoPoW proof (nipopowBootstrap = true, blocksToKeep >= 0) latched its
headers-synced flag and minimalFullBlockHeight while the proof was being applied: the floor,
max(stored, height - blocksToKeep + 1) rounded down to the voting-epoch start, landed in the proof's sparse prefix,
where the previous LastHeadersInContext - 1 headers are absent, so no full block was ever applicable.

Proof headers no longer schedule downloads while the proof is applied (nipopowMode); once the whole proof is
applied, the best stored proof header is checked once; updateBestFullBlock takes the lowest height a full block
connected to that header can be applied first at (the oldest connected header plus LastHeadersInContext - 1, never
inside a gap), rounding up to the next epoch start when needed. Nodes without NiPoPoW bootstrap, or with
blocksToKeep < 0, take the old path.

Tests (PopowProcessorSpecification): the floor is not inside the gap; it is the first height with
LastHeadersInContext connected headers (blocksToKeep beyond the suffix); a floor that would start mid-epoch moves to
the next epoch start and nothing below it is scheduled; a continuous chain keeps the floor it has without
nipopowBootstrap.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
